{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And it is driven back.</b> From a binyan whose verbal noun is not mentioned." "<b>And righteousness stands far off.</b> By way of parable, for its righteousness is not [truth]. אמת is feminine, and it is missing the letter nun, and [a parallel] is found contracted in the word אמתך (Isaiah 38:18)." "<b>And his reproof.</b> Things that a person says directly to his fellow. See דבריך טובים ונכוחים (II Samuel 15:13)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:18.953410078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}